  "Question": "Josanna’s test scores to date are \\(90,\\) \\(80,\\) \\(70,\\) \\(60,\\) and \\(85.\\) Her goal is to raise her test average at least \\(3\\) points with her next test. What is the minimum test score she would need to accomplish this goal?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(80\\)",
    "B": "\\(82\\)",
    "C": "\\(85\\)",
    "D": "\\(90\\)",
    "E": "\\(95\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "An average is the total divided by the number of tests, so first find Josanna's current total and average:\n\\[\n90+80+70+60+85=385,\\qquad \\frac{385}{5}=77.\n\\]\nHer new average must be at least \\(77+3=80\\). After the next test there will be six scores, so their total must be at least \\(6\\cdot80=480\\). She therefore needs at least\n\\[\n480-385=\\boxed{95}\n\\]\non the next test. A score of \\(95\\) gives exactly an \\(80\\) average, while any smaller score gives a smaller average. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
